summary:
All 14 acceptance criteria are met on this PC, at code level. The tree is the same one attempts 1 and 2 validated: HEAD is 6259427 and nothing outside .taad has changed. I re-ran every required check this attempt rather than citing the earlier ones:
- full suite: 689/692, with the same 3 last-access failures build-check saw before this slice;
- focused reveal and rule tests: 199/199;
- R-003 through the shipped exe: passed, no Explorer window opened;
- Fitness: 85 rules hold;
- rules-parity: AGREE 18/22/48;
- WindowMutants -Mutant All (Q-114): 12/12, and NoExplorerViewMember failed R-003 only on the armed check with reason=member;
- rules harness (Q-027): 117/117 AS-RECORDED, 0 stray hits;
- B-007, S-001 and S-006 at 560x644: passed, with 141 of 323 characters showing.

New this attempt: a probe for criterion 14, run against the real Core build on real files with the real shell parse (the open was faked). For a +H file, a +H+S file and a +H folder, deleting the item between the parse and the attribute read makes Walk count it as not hidden. It reads no view, calls the open once and frees the ID list once, which is what the design note says. The same items not deleted are refused under a 0|0 view without opening.

O-041 stays cannot-tell. Attempt 2 measured that shell32 keeps the view cached in each process. Whether Explorer's own Apply clears that cache in a running app needs a person to toggle Explorer's settings.

Explorer's actual selection behaviour was not observed. The exe now refuses before any open by design, and the landings (R-001/R-002), the Hidden=2 sitting and Windows 10 are left to a person.

Explorer's settings were Hidden=1, ShowSuperHidden=0 with 0 Explorer windows at every read. The probe folder and the mutant scratch folders are gone.

